o I got to looking at  how it's gonna pay for college for  mobile it's because I did I never had  that opportunity so we didn't go to  school I've always loved sales  I've always loved real estate so I  thought well if I can just get my  license and start selling real estate if  I can sell one house a month I can put  my kids through school without having to  go into debt and that's about time I  started listening to the Dave Ramsey  when I started with selling real estate  I also still worked out at the Klan and  at the time it was VP my job is a salary  job I go in at 6:00 in the morning I get  off at 4:30 in afternoon everybody wants  to see houses at nights and weekends so  that just kind of fell right in line  with it the first three months so I had  my real estate license I sold a million  dollars worth of real estate and now I  average selling about 30 to 35 houses or  properties a year I was able to quickly  both boys through school eight years of  college no debt  I told them if they would make the  grades I'd make the money and that's one  of the drives I've always had  [Music]  the chemical plant was still my bread  and butter  that's where my insurance was paid  that's where my benefits came from so I  started contributing at work I put in  10% of my pay into a 401k every time I  got a pay raise I bumped that up 1% well  I finally got up to where I spent 15  percent into my 401k the company was  matching 7% so that you know it's pretty  good a little nest egg going in and kind  of grew well then when BP sold out I was  over 50 years old I had been with the  company at least 20 years and so they  gave me a my pension they said that we  were eligible for a lump sum I looked at  it and was amazed at how much it had  grown it was a little over two hundred  fifty thousand so I took the lump sum  moved it down to Edward Jones talked to  my broker there and we made some  decisions on how we wanted to invest I  used a lot of Dave's principles on that  and I never really thought about being a  millionaire in fact I didn't even  realize until just recently when  listening to Dave on the radio you know  somebody asked him so well how do you  know when you get to the beat of meeting  their status and he said basically take  your assets add them up you know  subtract out what you owe and that tells  you where you're at and I went back and  looked at my 401k and I looked at the  IRA that I had set up with Edward Jones  and he came out to nine hundred twelve  thousand dollars when I realized that  that was nine hundred twelve thousand I  mean I just kind of floored me now that  I'm there I've decided I'm not gonna  quit working I want to be able to pass  on to my kids and to their kids a little  bit of a legacy and so to do that I'll  continue to work in both jobs  for the next four or five six years but  if I keep putting money into the savings  and keep letting it grow  it'll grow and five years down the road  who knows where I'll be  [Music]  if you make $20,000 a year you make  $40,000 here you make $200,000 here you  can get to that meeting that status if  you want to if you're willing to put a  little bit of money aside and live on  less than you make I'm proof if you  start at 35 you can do it it's just you  have to put a little bit more aside than  then you would have had to if you  started at 19 or 20 you're not going to  just jump in to where I am today but the  biggest thing is you've got to start  somewhere start start putting something  aside a little bit of time you can look  on Dave Ramsey site and find your  endorse local provider you can go there  talk to them about how much do I need to  start putting into a an IRA to get it  started and then just continue to do it  you've got to get started if you don't  start early you've got to get started at  some point I went from $14,000 a year to  now this last year I made $200,000 but I  work two full time jobs to do it you can  keep working at it and you can build $20  